# SLAAPS launch profile C: launcher stage (SLA_FLT_STAGE 2), operator-stick EDF, fixed gains modeled at 25 m/s indicated, schedule OFF.
# Written 2026-11-21. NOTHING HERE IS MEASURED. Load AFTER slaaps_vehicle.params and slaaps_canard_trims.params; apply with SLA_CFG_APPLY +1 disarmed.
#
# Launcher stage: Manual arms only with a fresh, valid raw airspeed sample (SLA_LAUNCH_AS_I). Canards stay at trim (no attitude authority) until
# indicated airspeed reaches SLA_LAUNCH_AS, then the attitude loop takes over. The control schedule is not supported in this stage
# (validateFlightConfiguration rejects SLA_SCH_EN 1): a launch starts at rest, outside the scheduled table.
# EDF: the operator pushes the throttle stick to full at launch (lead's decision 2026-11-21). Manual entry needs the stick low (SLA_EDF_ENTRY).
# SLA_EDF_RISE is NOT changed here: at 2.5 per second the EDF reaches full in 0.4 s. A harder step is the lead's decision after thrust-stand tests.
#
# SLA_LAUNCH_AS 20 m/s indicated: set by the project lead on 2026-11-21 (the basis is not recorded in this repository). It is INDICATED airspeed
# (about 22.4 m/s true at the 0.975 kg/m^3 site). Model check only: at 20 m/s the loop is at (20/25)^2 = 0.64 of its design authority, about damping 0.5.
# SLA_LAUNCH_AS_I 0: the pitot is airspeed instance 0 (measured on the board 2026-11-23, 'uorb top -1 airspeed').
# SLA_LAUNCH_AGE 250 ms: the DroneCAN DLVR publishes airspeed at 10 Hz (measured 2026-11-23), and timestamp_sample is about 28 ms older than the
# publication, so the sample age the check sees runs from about 28 to 128 ms. The earlier 100 ms failed for part of every period. In the launcher
# stage a fresh sample is needed to admit an arming. Since 2026-11-23 (LaunchAirspeed.hpp) a running session no longer needs one, but arming at the
# launcher still does, so 250 ms rides out one missed publication there. A reading down to -5 m/s is valid (zeroed-pitot noise).
# The pitot must read positive and true (boom fix confirmed 2026-11-21) and be zeroed at the launch temperature.
#
# Gains (same method as data revision 3): derivatives, SLA_x_M_SCALE and SP_ACC are the revision-3 (40 m/s) values x (25/40)^2 = 0.3906;
# RATE_P and RATE_I are divided by 0.3906. Best single design speed for 18..40 m/s indicated in the stability analysis (Tools/slaaps/stability_margin.py):
# stable from about 10 to 64 m/s indicated, worst-case damping 0.35 over 18..40. At the 20 m/s gate speed the modeled damping is about 0.5.
# Model only; the real canard authority and the launch-speed range are unmeasured.
# Revision 8 (2026-11-23) = revision 6 with SLA_LAUNCH_AGE 250 ms and the weighed mass 1.979 kg, restated here so the load order does not matter.
# Revision 10 (2026-11-23) = revision 8 with the body correction (modeled, slender-body theory, 85 mm body at the canards): canard
# derivatives, their uncertainties, SLA_x_M_SCALE and SP_ACC x 2.30 in pitch and yaw and x 2.95 in roll; RATE_P and RATE_I divided by
# the same factors. The isolated-canard values above (x 0.3906 of revision 3) are the starting point; the damping figures refer to them.
# Roll authority at the 20 m/s gate is then about 0.130 N m against the measured 0.05 N m EDF reaction torque. Not measured.
# This file sets SLA_DATA_REV 10 and SLA_DATA_STATE 0: the lead must declare it (SLA_DATA_STATE 1) before Manual can arm.
1	1	SLA_FLT_STAGE	2	6
